  "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented the payments system. Here's what was added:\n\n## Summary\n\n**New file: `src/payments.js`**\n- `recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })` \u2014 Records a payment on an issued or partially paid invoice. Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with the payment added to `invoice.payments` array (created if missing). Updates status to 'paid' when balance reaches zero, or 'partially_paid' while something is owed. Returns `fail()` for:\n  - `NOT_ISSUED` \u2014 if invoice isn't 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n  - `AMOUNT_INVALID` \u2014 if amount isn't a positive integer\n  - `OVERPAYMENT` \u2014 if payment exceeds amount owed\n\n- `balanceDue(invoice)` \u2014 Returns the remaining amount owed after subtracting all payments from the invoice total\n\n**Updated: `src/errors.js`**\n- Added `NOT_ISSUED` and `OVERPAYMENT` error codes\n\n**New test file: `test/payments.test.js`**\n- 19 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Balance calculations with no/partial/full payments\n  - Multiple payments\n  - Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n  - Validation (draft invoices, invalid amounts, overpayments)\n  - Immutability of original invoices\n\nAll 158 tests pass (139 existing + 19 new). The implementation follows all house rules: integer cents only, no mutation of arguments, proper error handling, and complete test coverage.",
